@startuml analyse-parcours-vue-generale
title Web journey analysis — Overview of the workflow (by theme)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  BorderColor #5BA1BC
  FontColor #1C2856
  DiamondBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
  DiamondBorderColor #5BA1BC
}
skinparam ArrowColor #5BA1BC
skinparam ActivityBarColor #5BA1BC
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #E0F0F4
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9BD0DD
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #ECECF2
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #5BA1BC
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam LegendBorderColor #000000
skinparam LegendFontSize 14

start

legend top right
  **Legend**

  <back:#ECECF2><color:#ECECF2>XXXXXX</color></back>  Pale grey background: automatic
  (machine calculation, no human action)

  <back:#9BD0DD><color:#9BD0DD>XXXXXX</color></back>  Light blue background: human action required
  (input, decision, or answer from an external third party)

  [ref] Reference doc: capture-har-and-coverage.md
  ../../.claude/skills/analyse-parcours/docs/
endlegend

partition "**MANUAL CAPTURE** [ref] (prerequisite, human, outside the skill)" #9BD0DD {
  :Network : Preserve log + Disable cache
  Full journey, cookies accepted
  -> "Save all as HAR with content" (.har);
  :Coverage panel (Cmd+Shift+P)
  Record, reload, scroll
  -> export JSON per page (Coverage-*.json);
}

note right #ECECF2
  cwv.json (Core Web Vitals) optional: Lighthouse
  launches automatically if absent (collect_cwv_pagespeed.py),
  or provided by the user (RUM/PageSpeed).
end note

partition "**COLLECTION** (automatic)" {
  :HAR, Coverage, Core Web Vitals
  (analyze_har.py, coverage_metrics.py,
  collect_cwv_pagespeed.py or run_lighthouse.sh as fallback);
}

partition "**AUTOMATIC EOF JUDGMENT** (automatic)" {
  :run_eof.py compares the already
  collected data against the EOF reference
  (~10 criteria out of 54 settled by script,
  the rest stays "I don't know");
}

partition "**CO2e IMPACT** (optional, at any time)" #9BD0DD {
  :/efootprint -> Boavizta model (reference
  + 3 cumulative scenarios prio1 / prio1+2 / prio1+2+3)
  -> data available for the NEXT
  report generation, not an isolated final add-on;
  :Possible human action: annual traffic and
  cloud instance size, if not auto-detected;
}

note right #ECECF2
  Can be launched before or after the first report,
  before or after the EOF questionnaire: each
  report generation simply picks up the
  data then available on disk.
end note

partition "**REPORT — first generation** (automatic)" {
  :generate_report_html.py
  (+ check_report_values.py, internal
  non-blocking check)
  -> already contains the automatic EOF judgment
  (partial) and the CO2e if already calculated;
}

partition "**EOF QUESTIONNAIRE** (manual, mission decision)" #9BD0DD {
  :When: after the automatic judgment,
  only on the criteria left
  "I don't know" - never before,
  never triggered on its own;
  :generate_questionnaire.py -> file to fill in
  (questionnaire-eof.md), sent to the client,
  filled in, read back (parse_questionnaire.py),
  merged (merge_lots.py) according to the
  precedence collected > estimated > stated
  > declared > assumed;
}

note right #ECECF2
  Trap to avoid: never rerun run_eof.py
  alone after a questionnaire read-back
  (it silently overwrites the answers). Always
  parse_questionnaire.py -> merge_lots.py
  -> generate_report_html.py.
end note

partition "**REPORT — regeneration** (automatic)" {
  :generate_report_html.py
  -> reflects the questionnaire answers
  merged (+ CO2e if calculated meanwhile);
}

stop

@enduml
